_template: news-item.jade
---
title: Announcing PyCascades 2020
---
author: PyCascades Team
---
date: 2019-07-18
---
meta_description: We'll meet in Portland, Oregon in 2020 for the third iteration of PyCascades.
---
body:

After an absolutely wonderful conference in Seattle, we're happy to announce that planning has begun for the third iteration of PyCascades. 🎉🎉🎉

For 2020, we'll meet up in Portland, Oregon 🇺🇸. Date and venue will be coming
soon, but we'll once again be aiming for early in the year.

As is now tradition a new year and new city means new organizers. It's our
pleasure to announce that **Eric Holscher** and **Esti Shay** will be leading
PyCascades 2020 as our co-chairs. You can read more about them on our
`organizers </organizers>`_ page or say hi 👋 to them
`on Slack <http://bit.ly/pycascades-slack>`_.

We want to put on an amazing show and make sure it's possible for all
people to attend. We're committed to continuing and expanding our opportunity
grants program. To make all this happen we're seeking
`sponsors </become-a-sponsor>`_. Please reach out to us at
organizers@pycascades.com if you're interested.

Finally, make sure to `subscribe to our newsletter </#newsletter>`_ to be the
first to hear about the confirmed dates, our call for talk submissions, when
tickets go on sale, and more.

✨ We're so excited to see you in Portland next year. ✨
